<% content_for :title, "Phoebe Zhu · Nalu" %>

<article class="who-am-i-page">
  <p class="who-am-i-page__back"><%= web_back_link %></p>
  <%= image_tag "phoebe_zhu_portrait.png",
      class: "who-am-i-page__portrait",
      alt: "Phoebe Zhu" %>

  <h1 class="who-am-i-page__name">PHOEBE ZHU</h1>
  <p class="who-am-i-page__place">New York, NY</p>

  <p class="who-am-i-page__bio">
    Hi, I’m Phoebe. I love traveling, seeing the world with fresh eyes, and discovering something new along the way - also a big fan of crisp mornings and good coffee.
  </p>

  <%= image_tag "phoebe_zhu_adventures.jpg",
      class: "who-am-i-page__adventures",
      alt: "Sunrise over the water and racing the Chicago triathlon" %>

  <p class="who-am-i-page__bio">
    Nalu (pronounced as “NAH-loo”) is a Hawaiian word for “wave” - also carries the idea of going with the flow, and reflecting.
  </p>

  <%= image_tag "phoebe_zhu_beach.png",
      class: "who-am-i-page__adventures who-am-i-page__adventures--last",
      alt: "Sunset waves on the beach" %>
</article>
